1
00:03:47,026 --> 00:04:17,006
We'll be right back.

2
00:04:17,026 --> 00:04:47,006
We'll be right back.

3
00:04:47,026 --> 00:05:17,006
We'll be right back.

4
00:05:17,026 --> 00:05:22,706
The End of the Legendary Man, the day the C-Train cried.

5
00:05:47,026 --> 00:05:48,846
Pleased to meet you, Your Honor.

6
00:05:49,786 --> 00:05:51,026
My name is Spandum.

7
00:05:51,086 --> 00:05:52,266
I'm with CP5.

8
00:05:52,366 --> 00:05:52,846
A pleasure.

9
00:05:53,146 --> 00:05:53,726
And thanks.

10
00:05:54,106 --> 00:05:54,946
You saved us.

11
00:05:55,506 --> 00:05:58,406
We can take over the investigation from here if you don't mind.

12
00:05:58,626 --> 00:06:00,406
We'll give them a full interrogation.

13
00:06:00,766 --> 00:06:00,906
Hmm.

14
00:06:01,686 --> 00:06:04,346
Just try talking your way out of this one.

15
00:06:04,686 --> 00:06:06,686
The trust they had in you has been shattered.

16
00:06:07,806 --> 00:06:11,406
Soon those blueprints for the ancient weapons will be mine.

17
00:06:12,086 --> 00:06:13,426
How could this happen?

18
00:06:13,426 --> 00:06:20,046
First off, about the C-Train.

19
00:06:20,586 --> 00:06:21,526
Magnificent work.

20
00:06:21,966 --> 00:06:25,206
With its help, Water 7 will continue to grow and flourish.

21
00:06:25,386 --> 00:06:29,846
For that, on the previous charge of building Gold Rogers' ship, your acquittal today had

22
00:06:29,846 --> 00:06:31,386
pretty much already been decided.

23
00:06:31,786 --> 00:06:36,486
Knowing that, why in the world would you commit such a heinous crime and erase that opportunity?

24
00:06:36,866 --> 00:06:37,946
Please, explain yourself.

25
00:06:38,026 --> 00:06:39,006
That's a lie!

26
00:06:39,186 --> 00:06:41,866
It wasn't Tom or any of us that attacked the judicial ship.

27
00:06:41,866 --> 00:06:43,326
It was that idiot Spandum!

28
00:06:43,506 --> 00:06:44,626
He's the one responsible!

29
00:06:51,646 --> 00:06:52,466
Ha ha ha!

30
00:06:52,586 --> 00:06:53,506
Sure it was!

31
00:06:53,626 --> 00:06:54,966
He's not serious, is he?

32
00:06:55,086 --> 00:06:56,806
What kind of crap is he trying to pull?

33
00:06:57,206 --> 00:07:01,426
Why would a government agency like CP5 attack a judicial ship?

34
00:07:01,546 --> 00:07:02,426
There's no way!

35
00:07:02,686 --> 00:07:06,006
You're gonna have to come up with a better lie than that, Mr. Apprentice.

36
00:07:06,006 --> 00:07:07,126
Ha ha ha ha!

37
00:07:07,626 --> 00:07:09,666
Your name is Cutty Flam, correct?

38
00:07:09,666 --> 00:07:14,086
I believe that was the name we took down from you when we caught you red-handed on board

39
00:07:14,086 --> 00:07:15,946
one of those treacherous raid ships.

40
00:07:16,306 --> 00:07:21,546
And correct me if I'm mistaken, but weren't those very same raid ships all made by your company?

41
00:07:26,006 --> 00:07:28,386
Ships that would do such a horrible thing.

42
00:07:32,906 --> 00:07:38,506
Something so awful are no longer my ships!

43
00:07:39,666 --> 00:07:49,286
Tom, pour off his chains!

44
00:07:49,366 --> 00:07:50,426
He's on a rampage!

45
00:07:50,486 --> 00:07:51,246
Take aim!

46
00:07:54,826 --> 00:07:56,226
He just hit him.

47
00:07:56,646 --> 00:07:58,706
Tom has never hit Frankie before.

48
00:07:59,606 --> 00:08:01,006
What'd you do that for?

49
00:08:01,006 --> 00:08:05,766
They're no longer your ships, huh?

50
00:08:07,086 --> 00:08:08,986
Don't you ever say that again!

51
00:08:10,326 --> 00:08:11,866
What's wrong with saying that?

52
00:08:12,046 --> 00:08:13,506
I wish I'd never made them!

53
00:08:13,506 --> 00:08:17,986
If those ships didn't exist, then nobody would have gotten hurt!

54
00:08:19,986 --> 00:08:24,126
When a ship is built, no matter what type,

55
00:08:24,626 --> 00:08:28,346
it's neither good nor evil.

56
00:08:29,966 --> 00:08:33,766
I don't care what kind of ship you choose to make for the rest of your life.

57
00:08:33,766 --> 00:08:37,646
Remember, even if the ships you build hurt someone,

58
00:08:38,026 --> 00:08:39,726
even if they destroy the world,

59
00:08:40,106 --> 00:08:41,406
even if no one else does,

60
00:08:41,466 --> 00:08:43,466
their creator must love them unconditionally.

61
00:08:43,846 --> 00:08:46,666
The one who made them must never deny them!

62
00:08:46,926 --> 00:08:48,706
Don't place the blame on the ships!

63
00:08:49,386 --> 00:08:50,926
You must be proud

64
00:08:50,926 --> 00:08:53,706
of every ship you've ever created!

65
00:08:53,706 --> 00:08:54,206
I'm dead!

66
00:09:04,366 --> 00:09:04,826
Papa!

67
00:09:13,626 --> 00:09:14,206
Iceberg.

68
00:09:15,286 --> 00:09:15,766
Frankie.

69
00:09:16,606 --> 00:09:17,806
Whatever happens,

70
00:09:18,026 --> 00:09:20,066
don't interfere with what I'm about to do.

71
00:09:20,626 --> 00:09:21,666
No matter what.

72
00:09:21,666 --> 00:09:26,086
It's the world government who pinned this crime on us,

73
00:09:26,206 --> 00:09:28,966
and it's the world government who will be the ones to judge it.

74
00:09:29,346 --> 00:09:31,706
There's no way for us to be cleared of these charges.

75
00:09:32,786 --> 00:09:33,546
It's over.

76
00:09:34,646 --> 00:09:37,086
It must be tough for you to see your innocent ships

77
00:09:37,086 --> 00:09:39,406
being used for something as horrible as this.

78
00:09:39,966 --> 00:09:41,746
I bet you really want to hit that guy.

79
00:09:42,246 --> 00:09:43,006
Don't you, Frankie?

80
00:09:43,006 --> 00:09:43,106
Frankie.

81
00:09:43,106 --> 00:09:54,526
What are you doing?

82
00:09:54,626 --> 00:09:56,286
He's going crazy again.

83
00:09:57,086 --> 00:09:58,506
What is he doing?

84
00:09:58,666 --> 00:09:59,626
Stop it, please.

85
00:09:59,746 --> 00:10:01,686
You're making things worse than they already are.

86
00:10:03,426 --> 00:10:05,106
Can you even comprehend

87
00:10:05,106 --> 00:10:08,306
the pain that you put that boy through?

88
00:10:08,306 --> 00:10:09,466
Fire!

89
00:10:14,106 --> 00:10:15,306
They shot him.

90
00:10:24,306 --> 00:10:25,966
Tom, no!

91
00:10:25,966 --> 00:10:27,306
Tom, no!

92
00:10:44,306 --> 00:10:45,206
Tom, no!

93
00:10:45,206 --> 00:10:49,406
Tranquilizers, huh?

94
00:10:52,206 --> 00:10:56,446
Not so tough now, are you?

95
00:10:56,566 --> 00:10:57,906
Serves you right, fish man!

96
00:10:59,046 --> 00:10:59,866
Tom, wait!

97
00:11:00,126 --> 00:11:01,366
Why are you doing this?

98
00:11:01,726 --> 00:11:03,326
What are you standing around for?

99
00:11:03,606 --> 00:11:05,306
Get over there and apprehend them!

100
00:11:05,426 --> 00:11:06,446
We're going to take Tom

101
00:11:06,446 --> 00:11:08,326
and every last one of his villainous workers

102
00:11:08,326 --> 00:11:09,606
down to Ellie's lobby!

103
00:11:10,066 --> 00:11:11,306
Who would have thought that Tom

104
00:11:11,306 --> 00:11:12,846
could be such a dangerous guy?

105
00:11:12,846 --> 00:11:14,466
What the hell was he thinking?

106
00:11:15,346 --> 00:11:16,646
Just what you'd expect

107
00:11:16,646 --> 00:11:18,766
from a man who sold his soul to pirates!

108
00:11:19,466 --> 00:11:20,986
He made those battleships

109
00:11:20,986 --> 00:11:22,666
and waited around for a chance like this

110
00:11:22,666 --> 00:11:23,266
to use them!

111
00:11:23,426 --> 00:11:25,166
How dare you talk about him like that,

112
00:11:25,226 --> 00:11:25,966
you bastards!

113
00:11:26,346 --> 00:11:26,666
Stop it!

114
00:11:27,906 --> 00:11:28,846
It's all right.

115
00:11:29,526 --> 00:11:30,006
Tom!

116
00:11:30,426 --> 00:11:31,706
I'd like to confess.

117
00:11:31,706 --> 00:11:32,126
Hmm?

118
00:11:32,986 --> 00:11:34,966
The raid on the judicial ship

119
00:11:34,966 --> 00:11:36,886
was led by me.

120
00:11:38,066 --> 00:11:39,106
That's not true!

121
00:11:39,286 --> 00:11:40,366
Why would you say that?

122
00:11:40,666 --> 00:11:42,166
But I have a request.

123
00:11:42,846 --> 00:11:44,506
Save your breath, fish man!

124
00:11:44,686 --> 00:11:46,266
Nobody gives a damn about your...

125
00:11:46,266 --> 00:11:47,706
Shut your mouth, CP-5!

126
00:11:49,006 --> 00:11:50,806
So, what is this request?

127
00:11:51,246 --> 00:11:52,666
If building the sea train

128
00:11:52,666 --> 00:11:54,546
was supposed to be considered a pardon

129
00:11:54,546 --> 00:11:55,966
for one charge against me,

130
00:11:56,506 --> 00:11:57,846
then I'd like to be pardoned

131
00:11:57,846 --> 00:11:59,086
for today's charges.

132
00:11:59,506 --> 00:11:59,706
Huh?

133
00:12:00,566 --> 00:12:02,286
Even if that request is granted,

134
00:12:02,446 --> 00:12:03,266
you'll be right back

135
00:12:03,266 --> 00:12:04,806
to where you were to begin with.

136
00:12:05,186 --> 00:12:06,826
With the charge of building a ship

137
00:12:06,826 --> 00:12:08,046
for the King of the Pirates,

138
00:12:08,146 --> 00:12:10,106
which will result in the maximum penalty.

139
00:12:10,106 --> 00:12:11,466
Sounds good.

140
00:12:11,606 --> 00:12:12,886
I like that better anyway.

141
00:12:13,486 --> 00:12:15,026
Giving a hand to that Roger guy

142
00:12:15,026 --> 00:12:16,566
is something I'll never forget.

143
00:12:16,906 --> 00:12:17,726
In fact,

144
00:12:18,106 --> 00:12:20,226
it's something I take great pride in!

145
00:12:22,406 --> 00:12:23,846
He's proud of that?

146
00:12:24,066 --> 00:12:25,986
I can't believe he'd make such a bold claim

147
00:12:25,986 --> 00:12:27,366
about something so despicable.

148
00:12:27,746 --> 00:12:28,346
Traitor!

149
00:12:28,906 --> 00:12:29,746
Fish man!

150
00:12:29,806 --> 00:12:30,826
You regret that!

151
00:12:31,146 --> 00:12:31,946
Why, Tom?

152
00:12:32,486 --> 00:12:33,286
Tell me!

153
00:12:33,866 --> 00:12:34,906
It's for the best.

154
00:12:35,846 --> 00:12:36,626
Now, listen.

155
00:12:37,166 --> 00:12:38,746
Don't blame yourself for this.

156
00:12:39,146 --> 00:12:41,186
I never thought the world government

157
00:12:41,186 --> 00:12:42,626
would go to such extremes

158
00:12:42,626 --> 00:12:43,606
to get the blueprints.

159
00:12:44,746 --> 00:12:46,266
And the situation with Roger

160
00:12:46,266 --> 00:12:47,726
only makes the matter worse.

161
00:12:47,986 --> 00:12:48,646
Even so,

162
00:12:48,726 --> 00:12:50,066
it doesn't have to be this way!

163
00:12:50,086 --> 00:12:51,126
No, it's fine.

164
00:12:51,646 --> 00:12:52,386
Look around you.

165
00:12:52,906 --> 00:12:54,566
Even if I'm charged with a crime

166
00:12:54,566 --> 00:12:55,846
from 14 years ago,

167
00:12:56,226 --> 00:12:57,546
nothing else about this town

168
00:12:57,546 --> 00:12:58,466
is the same now

169
00:12:58,466 --> 00:12:59,626
as it was back then.

170
00:12:59,966 --> 00:13:01,306
This island is alive

171
00:13:01,306 --> 00:13:02,206
and strong.

172
00:13:02,206 --> 00:13:04,086
Tom, this is only the beginning.

173
00:13:04,586 --> 00:13:05,786
No matter what ends up

174
00:13:05,786 --> 00:13:06,726
happening to me,

175
00:13:07,626 --> 00:13:09,066
I was still able

176
00:13:09,066 --> 00:13:10,226
to help this town.

177
00:13:11,666 --> 00:13:12,546
My dream

178
00:13:12,546 --> 00:13:14,826
has finally

179
00:13:14,826 --> 00:13:17,346
begun to run.

180
00:13:19,286 --> 00:13:20,806
Tom, don't please!

181
00:13:22,946 --> 00:13:23,986
Tom, no!

182
00:13:29,486 --> 00:13:30,126
Iceberg.

183
00:13:30,746 --> 00:13:31,146
Frankie.

184
00:13:32,206 --> 00:13:34,226
Take care of the blueprints.

185
00:13:35,946 --> 00:13:36,426
Kokoro.

186
00:13:37,046 --> 00:13:37,666
Yokozuna.

187
00:13:38,646 --> 00:13:39,446
Thank you

188
00:13:39,446 --> 00:13:40,966
for everything.

189
00:13:45,966 --> 00:13:47,266
The tranquilizers

190
00:13:47,266 --> 00:13:48,446
finally kicked in!

191
00:13:48,666 --> 00:13:49,506
Capture those three

192
00:13:49,506 --> 00:13:50,846
for the judicial ship attack!

193
00:13:50,886 --> 00:13:51,566
Yes, sir!

194
00:13:53,066 --> 00:13:53,906
Hold it.

195
00:13:53,906 --> 00:13:57,086
I'm amending the charges.

196
00:13:57,646 --> 00:13:59,326
For the crime of designing

197
00:13:59,326 --> 00:14:00,286
and building a ship

198
00:14:00,286 --> 00:14:01,186
for Gold Roger,

199
00:14:01,306 --> 00:14:02,346
the King of the Pirates,

200
00:14:02,666 --> 00:14:03,906
Tom and Tom alone

201
00:14:03,906 --> 00:14:04,786
will be apprehended

202
00:14:04,786 --> 00:14:06,226
and taken to Annie's lobby.

203
00:14:06,966 --> 00:14:07,806
That is all.

204
00:14:11,286 --> 00:14:12,246
What in the hell

205
00:14:12,246 --> 00:14:13,066
got into that old

206
00:14:13,066 --> 00:14:13,866
geezer's head?

207
00:14:14,346 --> 00:14:14,766
Whatever.

208
00:14:15,206 --> 00:14:16,766
I don't need his lackeys.

209
00:14:17,146 --> 00:14:18,506
Release those two apprentices!

210
00:14:18,506 --> 00:14:27,046
Tom can't be saved from this.

211
00:14:28,366 --> 00:14:29,446
It's the government

212
00:14:29,446 --> 00:14:30,306
we're up against.

213
00:14:30,666 --> 00:14:31,986
There's nothing we can do.

214
00:14:32,486 --> 00:14:33,146
Endure it.

215
00:14:33,706 --> 00:14:35,086
Tom traded his life

216
00:14:35,086 --> 00:14:35,766
for yours.

217
00:14:36,286 --> 00:14:37,046
If you make them

218
00:14:37,046 --> 00:14:37,546
your enemy,

219
00:14:37,686 --> 00:14:38,946
you won't be able to win

220
00:14:38,946 --> 00:14:40,246
no matter how many lives

221
00:14:40,246 --> 00:14:41,126
you have to give.

222
00:14:41,946 --> 00:14:42,666
Annie's lobby

223
00:14:42,666 --> 00:14:43,706
is the government's

224
00:14:43,706 --> 00:14:45,226
personal judicial island.

225
00:14:45,906 --> 00:14:47,386
Not one single person

226
00:14:47,386 --> 00:14:48,226
who's been sent

227
00:14:48,226 --> 00:14:49,406
to that dreadful place

228
00:14:49,406 --> 00:14:51,066
has ever been seen again.

229
00:14:52,086 --> 00:14:53,106
The sea train

230
00:14:53,106 --> 00:14:54,506
is ready for departure, sir.

231
00:14:54,766 --> 00:14:55,286
We can leave

232
00:14:55,286 --> 00:14:56,246
any time you like.

233
00:14:56,346 --> 00:14:56,946
Very good.

234
00:14:57,606 --> 00:14:58,206
Cocoa.

235
00:14:58,806 --> 00:14:59,406
Ha ha!

236
00:14:59,926 --> 00:15:01,086
Let's get moving, men.

237
00:15:01,646 --> 00:15:02,646
Load up the prisoner.

238
00:15:03,206 --> 00:15:04,126
I can't.

239
00:15:04,926 --> 00:15:06,526
This bloated fish man

240
00:15:06,526 --> 00:15:07,006
is going for

241
00:15:07,006 --> 00:15:08,326
a little train ride.

242
00:15:09,106 --> 00:15:10,306
Endure this!

243
00:15:12,666 --> 00:15:13,506
Hey!

244
00:15:16,806 --> 00:15:22,006
Stop it!

245
00:15:27,386 --> 00:15:28,646
Get out of the way!

246
00:15:28,866 --> 00:15:29,146
Oh!

247
00:15:29,486 --> 00:15:31,366
Really messed up his face!

248
00:15:31,586 --> 00:15:31,806
No!

249
00:15:31,886 --> 00:15:32,686
Tom's apprentice

250
00:15:32,686 --> 00:15:34,326
is the one on a rampage!

251
00:15:34,686 --> 00:15:35,126
No!

252
00:15:35,346 --> 00:15:35,706
Stop!

253
00:15:35,846 --> 00:15:36,506
I'd better get him!

254
00:15:36,706 --> 00:15:37,686
Capture that criminal!

255
00:15:38,146 --> 00:15:38,706
The rest of you,

256
00:15:38,826 --> 00:15:39,866
take Tom to the train!

257
00:15:40,526 --> 00:15:41,986
That's not gonna happen!

258
00:15:41,986 --> 00:15:44,046
Nobody's taking him anywhere!

259
00:15:44,406 --> 00:15:45,486
Fire at will!

260
00:15:46,966 --> 00:15:48,886
Tom's staying right here!

261
00:15:51,926 --> 00:15:53,106
Are you okay?

262
00:15:53,426 --> 00:15:54,266
After him!

263
00:15:55,386 --> 00:15:55,986
Hurry!

264
00:15:56,166 --> 00:15:56,766
Get out of here!

265
00:15:57,446 --> 00:15:58,046
Fire!

266
00:15:58,046 --> 00:16:10,466
Damn it!

267
00:16:10,546 --> 00:16:11,646
He got away!

268
00:16:12,326 --> 00:16:14,006
I'll get that cutty flam brat

269
00:16:14,006 --> 00:16:15,586
if it's the last thing I do!

270
00:16:15,786 --> 00:16:16,546
That little criminal

271
00:16:16,546 --> 00:16:18,066
will pay for what he's done!

272
00:16:18,266 --> 00:16:19,226
Mark my words,

273
00:16:19,366 --> 00:16:20,426
once this case is over,

274
00:16:20,606 --> 00:16:22,286
I'll have him sent to the gallows!

275
00:16:22,286 --> 00:16:23,146
Spot him!

276
00:16:23,226 --> 00:16:23,806
He's here!

277
00:16:24,006 --> 00:16:24,406
Now!

278
00:16:24,786 --> 00:16:24,906
It...

279
00:21:55,113 --> 00:22:12,113
夢見た僕らは間違いじゃないと信じて 荒く埋れる海原を渡って行ける

280
00:22:12,113 --> 00:22:21,113
誰よりも浮かんで 思いやりもあるけれど

281
00:22:21,113 --> 00:22:31,113
もしも君がこの船を降りて 違う世界にいたとしても

282
00:22:31,113 --> 00:22:40,113
最後にはきっと笑えるよ

283
00:22:42,113 --> 00:22:50,113
ご視聴ありがとうございました

284
00:22:50,113 --> 00:22:53,113
I've been looking forward to seeing you

285
00:22:53,113 --> 00:22:55,113
